N:testing-strategies
D:Own verification strategy and release confidence. Use when deciding which test layers matter, how to keep tests deterministic, and what evidence proves a change is safe enough to ship.
G:testing verification quality-gates contract-testing determinism
U[5]:
  Defining a project test portfolio
  Choosing evidence for a risky change
  Fixing flaky or low-signal test suites
  Adding contract or failure-path coverage
  Defining release confidence gates
S[5]{n,action}:
  1,Identify the change risk
  2,Choose the smallest sufficient test layers
  3,Protect determinism and isolation
  4,Cover critical failure paths
  5,Define release evidence
R[4]:
  Do not force one framework stack on every repo
  Do not confuse coverage percent with confidence
  Avoid timing-based flakiness
  Contract meaning stays with the external owner
